    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive alignment, headlined by the dual-threat production of **Trea Turner** (77.49) and **Kyle Schwarber** (74.47). Both benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Mikolas, who carries a 4.77 xERA; the combination of a positive park factor and a top-two batting order slot provides the highest floor on the team. **Kazuma Okamoto** (67.88) also warrants attention, as he leverages a strong platoon advantage against the lefty Peterson to anchor the utility spot. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** faces a difficult task against the elite stuff of Cease (2.97 xERA), his dynamic platoon profile and leadoff positioning keep his efficiency score at a solid 64.03, justifying the start despite the SP-skill penalty.\n\nThe most notable bench decision today involved **Carson Benge**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a 41.68 score. While **Carson Benge** possesses intrigue, the projected difficulty of facing the lefty Griffin, coupled with a lack of platoon leverage, forced him to the bench in favor of more efficient daily output from **Jacob Gonzalez** and **Colt Keith**. Meanwhile, **Hector Rodriguez** remains a high-upside play (55.61) despite a lower-middle order slot, largely due to an elite 0.578 xwOBA that suggests he is a prime candidate to overperform his raw projection.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in the matchups against stingy arms. **Christian Yelich** (52.10) faces a challenging outing against Ashcraft; while the platoon advantage is favorable, the combination of a lower-tier SP-skill impact and an annoying defensive drag from an elite catcher keeps him near the bottom of our starters. We are effectively sitting **Gary Sanchez** (37.54) and **Dillon Dingler** (34.23) as both fall below our required 40.0 efficiency floor, prioritizing the preservation of our daily game caps for players with higher situational ceilings. We continue to monitor **Yordan Alvarez**, who remains sidelined today due to a scheduled team off-day.",
